Chapter: SpikeCatMain
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Sky
  cites Poc chapter Spike
  cites Poc chapter SpikePrint

 SPIKE ONLY. THROWAWAY. The cat's two stills -- frozen in the road, and airborne
 mid-leap -- split off `SpikeMain`. The split is convenience rather than necessity
 now; `SpikePondMain`'s header says why.

 THESE TWO ARE THE PAIR WORTH HAVING ON BARE METAL. The leap is the port's one
 deliberate difference from the game (`b^0.75` where the game uses `pow(b, 0.7)`),
 so it is the frame whose numbers are the port's own rather than a transcription,
 and the third arm compares every one of them.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (scene-line "cat-frozen" u-cat-frozen)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-cat-frozen) 0)
    print-line-uni (scene-line "cat-leap" u-cat-leap)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-cat-leap) 0)
  end
